            <chunk name="Object" index="18">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">1c8cb315-a5f7-51bc-9f5f-f56e0358011c</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">README</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">TWISTING POLYGON TOWER

A regular polygon floor plate is repeated up a tower, each floor rotated a fixed share of a total twist, and the floors are lofted into a twisting mass - the simplest parametric tower.

HOW TO USE
1. 'Plate radius' and 'Plate sides' set the floor plate; 'Floors' the number of levels; 'Floor height' the spacing.
2. 'Total twist' is the rotation in degrees from bottom to top.
3. Bake the final Geometry parameter to get the tower surface.

YOU WILL LEARN
- Polygon on a plane
- Division: spreading a total value over a count
- Series for heights and angles
- Radians: Rotate wants radians
- Loft through stacked curves

READ THE CANVAS LEFT TO RIGHT
Green = inputs you change, coloured boxes = numbered steps, blue = results.

SOURCE
Owen Derby (oderby) - oderby/VVD
examples/versionTower.ghx @ 548fa5333b
Licence: MIT (see LICENCE panel)
Modified for the Almond parametric library: regrouped, relabelled and annotated; the geometric logic is unchanged.</item>
